                <pb facs="0255" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg205"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Risley to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>To prevent Texas fever, now prevailing in America, importation of live cattle or
                    fresh meat from that country is prohibited in Denmark. Does the disease exist? I
                    have protested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Risley.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
